{"title":"1962 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following sets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-values satisfy the inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4850189a033109be1479bcdea1fc23c0957370.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x^2 + x &lt; 6?\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/4407b894c71ca66df8c392f1dea2f20627ffe462.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -2 &lt; x &lt; \\frac{3}{2} \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ x &gt; \\frac{3}{2} \\text{ or } x &lt; -2 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ x &lt; \\frac{3}{2} \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{2} &lt; x &lt; 2 \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ x &lt; -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"727\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, subtract 6 from both sides of the inequality, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/1/d917ad4469e2282dcb62b73a929c9a3fc1dfec92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^2 + x - 6 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />.\nThis is a parabola that opens upward when graphed, it has a positive leading coefficient. So any negative x values must be between its x-axis intersections, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea782fad762536af17b16c58337811b0a4002eef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -2, 1.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />. The answer is A.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017102153\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.004 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.004 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 26/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1105/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:12143:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017102153 and revision id 288509. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}